<%# THE FIRST SCREEN EVERY REAL USER MEETS: no rules at all.

    ONE sentence, and it names only what exists today. §8's bottom half now exists — the
    suggestions panel below this frame proposes rules from entry history — so the third route is
    named here alongside the two screens a rule can be written from by hand. When the engine has
    nothing to propose, the panel says so in its own words rather than leaving this sentence
    pointing at an empty section.

    A frame rather than a blank page: an empty screen reads as something that failed to load. %>
<section class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded px-6 py-8 text-center">
  <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">No funding rules yet</h3>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 max-w-xl mx-auto">
    A rule claims part of every period's income for one envelope — accept one of the suggestions below, or
    add one from a
    <%= link_to "pool", pools_path, class: "text-brand-dark hover:text-brand underline" %> or a
    <%= link_to "category", categories_path, class: "text-brand-dark hover:text-brand underline" %>
    — and it appears here, in the order the money fills.
  </p>
</section>
